          {
            "text": "I wrote `{\"invariant_exists\": false}` to the answer file. I worked this out by reading the test only. I couldn't run it, and I didn't open `sympy/utilities/lambdify.py`.\n\nThe test calls `lambdify(x, sin(x) + x**2, \"math\")` and only checks that the result is `callable`. `lambdify` returns a newly generated Python function object each time, so the 10 runs give 10 distinct objects with different identities. The test never checks their outputs.\n\nThis is a judgement call about what \"identical\" means. If it means the generated functions behave the same, they are all equivalent and return the same numbers for the same input, so the answer would be `true`. I took \"returned value identical\" to mean the function object itself, which is not the same across runs.",
